			],
			"Message": "fix(Land): Advance submodules — Cocoon SCM args, Mountain URI fixes, Output typed window, Sky bridge routing\n\nAdvance all five Element submodules with SCM argument projection in Cocoon, URI reconstruction and IPC hardening in Mountain, typed Tauri 2 window API in Output, and live workbench service integration in Sky.\n\n**Cocoon** (`fix`): Replace blanket `arguments` strip in `SanitizeResourceState` with `ProjectArg` — a shallow copy that preserves only the safe primitive fields `vscode.git` handlers consult (`resourceUri`, URI POJO fields, `fsPath`, `external`, scalar metadata). Cycles from the Repository back-reference are naturally excluded. SCM resource commands now navigate to the intended file across all git integration features.\n\n**Mountain** (`fix`): Reconstruct full URI from vscode.Uri POJO by fallback priority — `external` → `scheme+authority+path+query+fragment` → `fsPath` → bare `path`, so non-file URIs like `rust-analyzer-diagnostics-view:` resolve correctly. Bump `$provideTreeChildren` timeout from 5s to 15s for cold multi-repo workspace scans. Route `localPty:processBinary` through `TerminalSendText` so clipboard paste and escape sequences reach the PTY. Forward `outputChannel.hide` to Sky as `sky://output/show { visible: false }` instead of no-op.\n\n**Output** (`fix`): Split `InvokeWindowCommand` into `StartDragging` and `ToggleMaximize`, each preferring the typed `@tauri-apps/api/window` JS API (which injects the correct window label) before falling back to raw `core.invoke` with an explicit `{ label }` payload. Drag and maximize now work reliably under Tauri 2.x.\n\n**Sky** (`fix`): Normalise output channel payload field names (`channel`/`name`/`handle`/`id`, `text`/`value`) across Mountain's coalescer, legacy append, and Cocoon forwarding paths. Route `sky://notification/show` through `INotificationService.notify()` for live toast rendering. Call `monaco.editor.setModelLanguage()` for `sky://languages/setDocumentLanguage`. Derive per-repo SCM display labels from `rootUri` basename in multi-repo workspaces. Route progress through `IProgressService.withProgress()` with DOM fallback during early boot.\n\n**Maintain** (`docs`): Advance Rust API documentation submodule pin — 362 files, +4951/−1426 lines of regenerated rustdoc covering Build, Eliminate, CLI, and Architecture modules.",
			"SHA": "034b8ea83fae5f2e83829f7877f71d3829c4df71"
		},
